  "notes": [
    {
      "row": "notes",
      "title": "Why a step costs two forward passes",
      "text": "guide_scale > 1 means the DiT runs twice per step — once with the prompt, once without. That is why N = 40 steps is 80 model calls. Wan2.2-A14B adds a third wrinkle, swapping between a high-noise and a low-noise expert at a boundary timestep; the 1.3B model has a single DiT and skips that.",
      "code": [
        {
          "role": "call_site",
          "src": "wan.t2v",
          "lines": [
            346,
            349
          ],
          "expect": {
            "symbol": "WanT2V.generate",
            "first": "model = self._prepare_model_for_timestep(",
            "sha": "cc039940",
            "span": [
              208,
              383
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "row": "notes",
      "title": "What persists across steps, and what does not",
      "text": "context and context_null are computed once before the loop and never change. latents is the only state carried from step to step. Nothing is cached inside the model — every step re-attends the whole 32760-token sequence from scratch.",
      "code": [
        {
          "role": "definition",
          "src": "wan.t2v",
          "lines": [
            335,
            339
          ],
